  "verbalization": "Cefalotin is linked to Urinary Tract Infection (UTI) through a series of indications that ultimately converge on this disease. The evidence suggests that Cefalotin is used to treat Arthropathy, a condition that is itself indicated for Cefradine, Azlocillin, and Cefamandole. These antibiotics are all part of the broader class of cephalosporins, which are commonly used to combat bacterial infections, including UTIs. The shared indication chain implies a potential mechanism of action that targets bacterial pathogens, though the exact mechanism of action for Cefalotin is not fully elucidated in the provided data. The integration of these indications suggests that Cefalotin may be repurposed for UTI treatment, though further research is needed to confirm its efficacy and safety in this context.",
